var e=[{id:1,slug:`acne`,title:`Acne & Breakouts`,shortDescription:`Comprehensive management for active acne and prevention strategies.`,overview:`Acne is a common skin condition that occurs when hair follicles become plugged with oil and dead skin cells. It can affect individuals of all ages and vary in severity.`,symptoms:[`Whiteheads`,`Blackheads`,`Papules`,`Pimples`,`Nodules or cystic lesions`],causes:[`Excess oil (sebum) production`,`Hair follicles clogged by oil and dead skin cells`,`Bacteria`,`Inflammation`],approach:`We offer personalized treatment plans ranging from topical prescriptions to advanced clinical therapies to manage active breakouts and prevent future acne.`,icon:`Droplet`},{id:2,slug:`pigmentation`,title:`Pigmentation & Melasma`,shortDescription:`Targeted solutions for uneven skin tone, dark spots, and melasma.`,overview:`Hyperpigmentation occurs when patches of skin become darker in color than the normal surrounding skin. This is usually harmless but can be a cosmetic concern.`,symptoms:[`Dark patches on the face or body`,`Uneven skin tone`,`Sun spots or age spots`],causes:[`Sun exposure`,`Hormonal influences`,`Age`,`Skin injuries or inflammation`],approach:`Our clinic utilizes advanced laser treatments, clinical peels, and specialized topical regimens to safely and effectively reduce pigmentation.`,icon:`Sun`},{id:3,slug:`hair-loss`,title:`Hair Loss (Alopecia)`,shortDescription:`Evaluation and advanced treatments for various types of hair loss.`,overview:`Hair loss can affect just your scalp or your entire body, and it can be temporary or permanent. It can be the result of heredity, hormonal changes, medical conditions or a normal part of aging.`,symptoms:[`Gradual thinning on top of head`,`Circular or patchy bald spots`,`Sudden loosening of hair`],causes:[`Family history (heredity)`,`Hormonal changes and medical conditions`,`Medications and supplements`,`Stress`],approach:`We provide thorough diagnostics, including scalp analysis, followed by treatments like PRP, mesotherapy, or specialized medication to promote regrowth.`,icon:`Scissors`},{id:4,slug:`eczema`,title:`Eczema & Dermatitis`,shortDescription:`Care plans to soothe inflammation and manage flare-ups.`,overview:`Eczema is a condition that makes your skin red and itchy. It is common in children but can occur at any age.`,symptoms:[`Dry skin`,`Itchy skin (especially at night)`,`Red to brownish-gray patches`,`Thickened, cracked, scaly skin`],causes:[`Immune system activation`,`Genetics`,`Environmental triggers`,`Stress`],approach:`We focus on restoring the skin barrier, identifying triggers, and using targeted therapies to keep flare-ups under control.`,icon:`Activity`},{id:5,slug:`psoriasis`,title:`Psoriasis`,shortDescription:`Advanced management for psoriasis flare-ups and long-term care.`,overview:`Psoriasis is a skin disease that causes a rash with itchy, scaly patches, most commonly on the knees, elbows, trunk and scalp.`,symptoms:[`Red patches of skin covered with thick, silvery scales`,`Small scaling spots`,`Dry, cracked skin that may bleed or itch`,`Itching, burning or soreness`],causes:[`Immune system problem`,`Genetics`,`Infections`,`Stress and environmental factors`],approach:`We offer a range of treatments from topical ointments to advanced biologic therapies designed to clear the skin and manage symptoms effectively.`,icon:`Activity`},{id:6,slug:`rosacea`,title:`Rosacea`,shortDescription:`Expert care for managing facial redness and visible blood vessels.`,overview:`Rosacea is a common skin condition that causes redness and visible blood vessels in your face. It may also produce small, red, pus-filled bumps.`,symptoms:[`Facial redness`,`Swollen, red bumps`,`Eye problems (ocular rosacea)`,`Enlarged nose`],causes:[`Genetics`,`Environmental factors`,`Spicy foods or hot drinks`,`Sun exposure`],approach:`We create custom plans using gentle skincare routines, prescription medications, and specialized laser therapies to reduce redness and manage flare-ups.`,icon:`Sun`},{id:7,slug:`skin-cancer`,title:`Skin Cancer Screening`,shortDescription:`Comprehensive mole mapping and early detection of skin cancers.`,overview:`Skin cancer is the abnormal growth of skin cells, most often developing on skin exposed to the sun, but it can also occur on areas of your skin not ordinarily exposed to sunlight.`,symptoms:[`A pearly or waxy bump`,`A flat, flesh-colored or brown scar-like lesion`,`A large brownish spot with darker speckles`,`A mole that changes in color, size or feel`],causes:[`Ultraviolet (UV) radiation`,`Fair skin`,`History of sunburns`,`Family history of skin cancer`],approach:`We provide thorough full-body skin exams and mole mapping to detect early signs of melanoma and non-melanoma skin cancers, offering prompt surgical and medical interventions.`,icon:`Search`},{id:8,slug:`warts-moles`,title:`Warts & Moles Removal`,shortDescription:`Safe, effective removal of benign skin growths and lesions.`,overview:`Warts are small, grainy skin growths caused by a virus, while moles are common skin growths made of clusters of pigmented cells. Both are usually harmless but can be a nuisance.`,symptoms:[`Small, fleshy, grainy bumps`,`Flesh-colored, white, pink or tan growths`,`Rough to the touch`,`Dark brown spots (moles)`],causes:[`Human papillomavirus (HPV) for warts`,`Clusters of melanocytes for moles`,`Sun exposure`,`Genetics`],approach:`Our clinic utilizes cryotherapy, laser removal, or minor surgical excision to safely remove these growths with minimal scarring and discomfort.`,icon:`Scissors`}];export{e as t};